How to fix:
Treat a refusal and a genesis the invite does not name as that peer's answer rather than the Garden's: record it, drop that peer from consideration, and keep waiting for the other addresses the invite carries until the deadline. Fail only when no peer has admitted the node by the end of the bootstrap window, and include the refusing peer's identity in the error so an operator can see which invite entry is at fault. Add a regression test in which the first invite peer answers `Refused` (and one that answers with a swapped genesis) and a later peer admits the joiner, asserting the join succeeds.

Please fix this vulnerability. If you propose a fix, make it concise and minimal.
`````
