How to fix:
Bind authorship to the origin of the bytes rather than to the sender of a claim: have the publishing member sign the deposit of its content, record which validator deposited each content id, and take the object author from that deposit, refusing any `Publish` whose sender is not the depositor.

Until the content id itself commits to its author, a contested content id must not be writable at all: a block may not record an object for a content id that two different senders claim in the same pool, so a forged attribution is never committed and the honest publisher keeps a retry instead of losing the transaction permanently.

Add regression coverage for the two-sender, one-content-id case at both the state-machine and node levels.

Please fix this vulnerability. If you propose a fix, make it concise and minimal.
