### 🟡 Garden domain ids are not reserved in the settlement registry, so a third party can squat one and shadow a Garden's Budlum record

**Severity:** MEDIUM · Deep review

**TL;DR:** `garden_domain_id` derives a Garden's settlement domain id in the same id space the permissionless `SettlementTx::RegisterDomain` transaction writes to, and `consensus_domains_with_garden` lists canonical records before node-local Garden records, so a squatter's registration of that id wins every read of the Garden's own record.

**Impact:** Any client that can read a Garden node's public domain list, or simply hold the invite, can register a canonical settlement domain on that Garden's derived id. Every node that links the Garden afterwards skips its own registration, sums the squatter's record into `bud_gardenStatus`, and has every later Garden-to-Budlum report refused, so that Garden's finality is never recorded on Budlum again and the id cannot be reclaimed without founding a new Garden.

**Root cause:**
